"The letters Tā, Hā are like the disjointed letters (huruf al-muqatta'at) at the beginning of similar surahs; Allah knows best their meaning. While some commentators state that these are an oath by one of the beautiful names of Allah, others have narrated that it means 'ya rajul' (O man). It has also been explained that the expression 'Tā Hā' is a command addressed to the Prophet (peace be upon him) meaning 'put your foot down' or 'tread upon the ground.' For the Messenger of Allah would stand on one foot because he became very weary in the tahajjud prayer; with this command, he was asked to worship comfortably on both feet. 'Sirr' (secret) is what you say to yourself within; 'akhfa' (more hidden) is that which will happen but has not yet happened. Or, sirr is what is whispered secretly to another, while akhfa is what a person conceals within oneself. In addition, 'akhfa' has been interpreted as a past-tense verb meaning 'He concealed.'\n\nMoses (Musa) had told his family that he saw a fire and wanted to bring an ember or a guide from it. When he reached the fire, He decreed: 'O Moses! Indeed, I am your Lord; remove your sandals, for you are in the sacred valley of Tuwa. I have chosen you, so listen to what is revealed. Indeed, I am Allah; worship Me and establish prayer for My remembrance. The Hour is certainly coming—I keep its time hidden so that every soul may be recompensed for what it strives. Let not the one who disbelieves in it and follows his desires turn you away from it, lest you perish.' Then He asked Moses about his staff and his hand; the staff turned into a snake, and his hand came out shining white. These are among the greatest miracles. When he was commanded to go to Pharaoh, Moses said: 'My Lord! Expand for me my breast, ease my task for me, and untie the knot from my tongue so that they may understand my speech; appoint for me a minister from my family, my brother Aaron; reinforce my back through him, and make him an associate in my mission so that we may glorify You much and remember You much.' Allah said: 'O Moses! What you requested has been granted to you. We had already bestowed favor upon you once before: We inspired your mother to put Moses into a chest and cast it into the river, and the river would cast it onto the bank, where an enemy of Mine and an enemy of his would take him. And I cast over you love from Me. Your sister offered to find someone who would nurse him, and thus We returned you to your mother. You had killed a man, and We saved you from sorrow; We tested you with various trials, you stayed in Midian for years, and then you arrived at a designated time. I have chosen you for Myself. Go, you and your brother, with My signs, and do not slacken in remembering Me. Go to Pharaoh, for he has indeed transgressed. Speak to him with gentle words, perhaps he may take heed or fear.' When (Moses and Aaron) said they feared, Allah said: 'Do not fear, I am with you both, hearing and seeing.' Say to them: 'We are the messengers of your Lord; let the Children of Israel go with us and do not torment them. We have come to you with a sign from your Lord. Peace be upon those who follow guidance. It has been revealed to us that the punishment is upon whoever denies the truth and turns away.' Pharaoh said: 'Who is your Lord?' Moses said: 'Our Lord is the One who gave everything its form, then guided it.' Pharaoh said: 'What is the state of the past generations?' Moses said: 'Knowledge of them is with my Lord in a record. My Lord neither errs nor forgets. It is He who made the earth a cradle, opened pathways therein, and sent down water from the sky; with that water We produced pairs [of various plants]. Eat, and pasture your cattle. Indeed, in that are signs for people of understanding.'\n\nFrom the earth We created you, into it We shall return you, and from it We shall bring you forth once more. And We certainly showed Pharaoh all of Our signs, but he denied and refused to accept. Pharaoh said: 'O Moses! Have you come to drive us out of our land with your magic? Then we will surely come to you with magic like it; appoint a meeting between us at an agreed time and place.' Moses said: 'The day of the festival (day of adornment), and let the people be assembled at mid-morning.' Pharaoh went away, gathered his schemes and resources. Moses said to them: 'Woe to you! Do not fabricate a lie against Allah, lest He eradicate you with a punishment. Whoever invents a falsehood is surely ruined.' The magicians disputed among themselves secretly: 'These two are surely magicians; they want to drive you out of your land and destroy your exemplary way of life. Gather your schemes together, then come forward in line; whoever prevails today has won.' The magicians said: 'O Moses! Either you cast, or we will be the first to cast.' Moses said: 'No, you cast.' Due to their magic, their ropes and staffs seemed to him as though they were moving; Moses felt a fear within himself. We said: 'Do not fear; you are the one who is superior. Cast what is in your right hand; it will swallow what they have made. What they have made is merely a magician's trick. And a magician will not succeed wherever he may go.' Thereupon the magicians fell down in prostration, saying: 'We believe in the Lord of Moses and Aaron.' Pharaoh said: 'Did you believe in him before I gave you permission? He must be your chief who taught you magic. I will certainly cut off your hands and your feet on opposite sides, and I will crucify you on the trunks of palm trees; then you will surely know which of us is more severe and enduring in punishment.' They said: 'We will never prefer you over the clear signs that have come to us and the One who created us. So decree whatever you will decree; you can only decree over this worldly life. We have believed in our Lord so that He may forgive our sins and the magic you forced upon us. Allah is better in reward and more enduring in punishment.' Whoever comes to his Lord as a criminal, indeed, for him is Hell; he will neither die therein nor live. But whoever comes to Him as a believer having performed righteous deeds, for such there will be the highest ranks, the Gardens of Eden beneath which rivers flow, abiding eternally therein. Such is the reward of those who purify themselves.'\n\nWe revealed to Moses (Musa): 'Travel by night with My servants, strike for them a dry path across the sea; do not fear being overtaken, nor be apprehensive of drowning.' Pharaoh pursued them with his armies, and the sea engulfed them completely. Thus Pharaoh led his people astray. O Children of Israel! We delivered you from your enemy, made an appointment with you on the right side of Mount Tur, and sent down upon you manna and quails. Eat from the pure provisions We have provided for you, and do not transgress, lest My wrath descend upon you; and whomever My wrath descends upon has surely perished. Yet surely I am All-Forgiving toward whoever repents, believes, works righteousness, and then remains steadfast on the true path. Allah said: 'O Moses! What made you hasten ahead of your people?' Moses said: 'They are following in my footsteps, and I hastened to You so that You might be pleased.' Allah said: 'Indeed, We have tested your people after your departure, and the Samiri has led them astray.' Moses returned to his people, angry and sorrowful: 'O my people! Did your Lord not make you a good promise? Did the time seem too long to you, or did you desire that wrath from your Lord should descend upon you, so you broke your promise to me?' They said: 'We did not break our promise to you of our own accord; rather, we were laden with burdens of ornaments of that people, so we cast them away, and the Samiri likewise threw his.' Finally, the Samiri brought out for them the statue of a calf that lowed. The Samiri and his followers said: 'This is your god and the god of Moses, but he forgot.' Did they not see that it could not return a word to them, nor could it bring them harm or benefit? Indeed, Aaron had previously said: 'O my people! You have only been tested by this; your true Lord is the Most Compassionate (al-Rahman); so follow me and obey my command.' They said: 'We will continue worshipping it until Moses returns to us.' When Moses arrived, he said: 'O Aaron! What prevented you, when you saw them going astray? Why did you not follow my way? Did you disobey my command?' Aaron said: 'O son of my mother! Do not seize me by my beard or by my head. I feared that you would say, \"You caused division among the Children of Israel and did not heed my word.\"' Moses said to the Samiri: 'O Samiri! What is this you have done?' The Samiri said: 'I saw something they did not see: I took a handful of dust from the track of the divine messenger and threw it into the molten ornaments; thus did my soul entice me.' Moses said: 'Then begone! Your lot in this life is to say, \"Touch me not\"; and indeed, you have an appointed punishment from which you cannot escape. Now look at your god to which you remained devoted; we will surely burn it, reduce it to ashes, and scatter it into the sea.' Your only God is Allah, besides Whom there is no deity; His knowledge encompasses all things. O Muhammad! Thus do We relate to you the accounts of the past; and We have granted you from Our presence a Reminder (the Quran). Whoever turns away from it will bear a burden of sin on the Day of Resurrection, remaining under its punishment perpetually. On the Day the Trumpet (Sur) is blown, We will gather the criminals with their eyes turned blue. They will whisper among themselves: 'You stayed in the world for only ten (days).' The one most perceptive in judgment among them will say: 'You stayed for only a single day.'\n\nThey ask you about the mountains; say: 'My Lord will crumble them to dust and scatter them, leaving their places as a level, barren plain; you will see in it neither depression nor elevation.' On that Day, they will follow the summoner without deviation; voices will be hushed before the majesty of the Most Compassionate (al-Rahman), and you will hear nothing but a faint whisper. On that Day, no intercession will benefit except from one whom the Most Compassionate has permitted and whose word He is pleased with. Allah knows what lies ahead of them and what is behind them, but they cannot encompass Him in knowledge. All faces will be humbled before Allah, the Ever-Living, the All-Sustaining; and whoever bears a burden of wrongdoing has surely ended in ruin. Whoever does righteous deeds while being a believer will fear neither injustice nor deprivation. Thus have We sent it down as an Arabic Quran and varied warnings in it, so that perhaps they may fear Allah or it may serve as a reminder for them. Exalted is Allah, the True Sovereign whose decree prevails over all. Do not hasten with reciting the Quran before its revelation is completed to you, and say: 'My Lord, increase me in knowledge!' We had previously commanded Adam, but he forgot, and We found no firm resolve in him. When We said to the angels: 'Prostrate before Adam,' they all prostrated except Iblis; he refused. We said: 'O Adam! Indeed, this is an enemy to you and to your wife; so let him not drive you both out of Paradise, lest you become wretched. Truly, it is granted to you that you will neither go hungry nor go naked in Paradise; nor will you thirst there or suffer the blazing heat.' Then Satan whispered to him, saying: 'O Adam! Shall I show you the tree of eternity and a kingdom that never decays?' They both ate from that tree, and their nakedness became visible to them, so they began to fasten the leaves of Paradise over themselves. Adam disobeyed his Lord and went astray. Then his Lord chose him, accepted his repentance, and guided him. Allah said: 'Descend from it, all of you, enemies to one another; then whenever guidance comes to you from Me, whoever follows My guidance will not go astray nor suffer hardship. And whoever turns away from My remembrance will have a constricted life, and We will gather him blind on the Day of Resurrection.' He will say: 'My Lord, why have You gathered me blind when I used to see?' Allah will say: 'Thus it is; Our verses came to you and you forgot them; and so today you are forgotten.' Thus do We requite whoever exceeds the bounds and does not believe in the verses of his Lord; and the punishment of the Hereafter is far more severe and enduring. Has it not guided them to see how many generations We destroyed before them, through whose dwellings they walk? Surely in that are signs for people of understanding. Had it not been for a prior word from your Lord and a term already fixed, the punishment would have overtaken them immediately. So be patient with what they say, and glorify your Lord with praise before the rising of the sun and before its setting, and glorify Him during hours of the night and at the ends of the day, so that you may attain contentment. Do not extend your eyes toward that which We have bestowed upon various groups of disbelievers as the splendor of worldly life to test them; the provision of your Lord is far better and more enduring. Enjoin prayer upon your family and patiently persevere in it; We do not ask you for provision, We provide for you. And the good end is for the righteous. Those who disbelieve say: 'Why does he not bring us a miracle from his Lord?' Has there not come to them clear proof of what was in the earlier scriptures? If We had destroyed them with a punishment before this, they would surely have said: 'Our Lord, why did You not send us a messenger so that we could have followed Your verses before being humiliated and disgraced?' Say: 'Each is waiting, so wait; you will surely know who the companions of the even path are and who is rightly guided.'"